# Cursor Rules

- Always consult `AGENTS.md` for repository conventions and skill structure standards.
- When working within or invoking skills from `JobApplications/`, follow `JobApplications/AGENTS.md`:
  - Profile is stored in `job-work/profile.md` (generated by `resume-parse`).
  - Search postings against profile via `job-search`.
  - Draft applications via `apply-to-job` (answers cached in `job-work/answers.md`).
  - Never hallucinate resume details; always require user approval before submitting anything.
- When applying Software Engineering methodologies, consult `swe/AGENTS.md` for process model selection and step execution:
  - Enforce the **Agentic-First Critique**: Start with modern agentic frameworks (`/swe-agent-loop` for bug fixes, `/spec-driven-dev` for features, `/multi-agent-sop` for multi-role workflows, `/agentic-sdlc` for repo lifecycles).
  - Fall back to classical models (`/v-model`, `/waterfall`, `/spiral-model`, `/scrum`, `/cleanroom`) only when specific compliance, contract, or zero-defect constraints dictate.
  - Declare the selected model and justification before writing code.
- Run `python scripts/validate-skills.py` locally before proposing changes.
